8,8,8,6,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,6,6,6,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"**What the grid contains.** Each input has two kinds of things:\n- **One multi-cell shape**, in colour A. The shapes are a 3×3 \"2\" in pair 1, a 4×3 \"1\" in pair 2, a 3×3 \"4\" in pair 3, and a 4×3 \"6\" in the test.\n- **A small constellation of single dots**, spaced 2 cells apart. Exactly one dot has the shape's colour A; I call it the centre dot. All the other dots share a second colour B.\n\n**What the output does.** The constellation is a small map of where copies of the shape go.\n- The centre dot stands for the shape's original position. The shape stays there, but it is recoloured to B.\n- Every B dot stands for a copy of the shape in colour A. A dot at offset (dy, dx) from the centre dot gives a copy shifted by (dy/2 · shape height, dx/2 · shape width). So each dot step of 2 cells becomes one shape-sized step.\n- All the dots are erased.\n\n**Checking this against the pairs:**\n- **Pair 1.** The 3×3 shape is at (3,12) and the centre dot at (8,4).\n  - The 8-dots at (6,4), (8,2), (8,6), (10,4) and (12,4) give copies at (0,12), (3,9), (3,15), (6,12) and (9,12).\n  - The original spot turns 8.\n  - This matches the output.\n- **Pair 2.** The 4×3 shape is at (6,5) and the centre dot at (13,15).\n  - The 2-dots at (11,13), (11,15), (11,17) and (15,15) give copies at (2,2), (2,5), (2,8) and (10,5).\n  - The original turns 2.\n  - This matches.\n- **Pair 3.** This pair fits the same rule. Copies that would run past the left edge are clipped there.\n\n**Test.** The 4×3 shape of 6 is at (5,8), and the centre dot (colour 6) is at (14,6). The 4-dots map as follows:\n\n| 4-dot | Copy of the shape in 6 at |\n|---|---|\n| (12,8) | (1,11) |\n| (14,2) | (5,2) |\n| (14,4) | (5,5) |\n| (14,8) | (5,11) |\n| (16,2) | (9,2) |\n\nThe original shape at (5,8) becomes colour 4, and the dots are erased.\n\n**Program outline.**\n1. Find the largest object; that is the shape.\n2. The single-cell objects are the dots. The one with the shape's colour is the centre dot.\n3. Take the dot spacing from the gcd of the dot offsets (it is 2 in every example).\n4. Stamp the copies, clipping at the grid edges, and emit a canvas after each stage.","code":"import math\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    shape = max(objs, key=lambda o: o[\"size\"])\n    A = shape[\"colour\"]\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = shape[\"box\"]\n    h, w = y1 - y0 + 1, x1 - x0 + 1\n    mask = crop(g, y0, x0, y1, x1) == A\n    dots = [o for o in objs if o[\"size\"] == 1]\n    centre = [o for o in dots if o[\"colour\"] == A][0]\n    cy, cx = centre[\"cells\"][0]\n    others = [o for o in dots if o is not centre]\n    B = others[0][\"colour\"]\n    step = 0\n    for o in others:\n        y, x = o[\"cells\"][0]\n        step = math.gcd(step, math.gcd(abs(y - cy), abs(x - cx)))\n    step = step or 1\n\n    out = g.copy()\n    for o in dots:\n        y, x = o[\"cells\"][0]\n        out[y, x] = bg\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Erase the dot constellation; it only serves as a placement map.\")\n\n    def stamp(oy, ox, colour):\n        for dy in range(h):\n            for dx in range(w):\n                if mask[dy, dx]:\n                    yy, xx = oy + dy, ox + dx\n                    if 0 <= yy < H and 0 <= xx < W:\n                        out[yy, xx] = colour\n\n    stamp(y0, x0, B)\n    emit(out.copy(), \"The centre dot (shape colour) marks the original shape: recolour it to the dot colour.\")\n    for o in others:\n        y, x = o[\"cells\"][0]\n        oy = y0 + (y - cy) // step * h\n        ox = x0 + (x - cx) // step * w\n        stamp(oy, ox, A)\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Dot at ({y},{x}) -> copy of the shape in colour {A} at ({oy},{ox}).\")\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Final arrangement.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Find the largest object; that is the shape."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The shape stays there, but it is recoloured to B."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"The centre dot (shape colour) marks the original shape: recolour it to the dot colour."}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"A dot at offset (dy, dx) from the centre dot gives a copy shifted by (dy/2 · shape height, dx/2 · shape width)."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp the copies, clipping at the grid edges, and emit a canvas after each stage."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"3a7534a4b85b7d307cac2aa40584cd5e16f038a379e7a57187bd46ec3d4a231c","task_sha256":"be3abd8ef585a416e73d875a8ece4489b29950ecae49becaa210421d7e3956cc","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
